WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.176
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.476 --> 00:00:08.897
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.197 --> 00:00:16.227
Unit twenty-seven: First Conditional (if + will). Today you will talk about real possibilities in the future.

4
00:00:16.527 --> 00:00:19.225
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:23.400
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:24.880
If.

7
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:28.289
If means a word that starts a condition.

8
00:00:28.883 --> 00:00:30.802
If it rains, we will stay.

9
00:00:31.417 --> 00:00:33.848
Your turn. Say: If.

10
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:37.376
If.

11
00:00:38.117 --> 00:00:39.002
Will.

12
00:00:40.017 --> 00:00:42.109
Will means used for a future result.

13
00:00:42.717 --> 00:00:43.845
I will call you.

14
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.719
Your turn. Say: Will.

15
00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:50.428
Will.

16
00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:51.975
Won't.

17
00:00:52.983 --> 00:00:54.344
Won't means will not.

18
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.172
We won't go out.

19
00:00:56.783 --> 00:00:58.878
Your turn. Say: Won't.

20
00:01:01.733 --> 00:01:02.549
Won't.

21
00:01:03.283 --> 00:01:04.668
Real possibility.

22
00:01:05.683 --> 00:01:08.855
Real possibility means something that may really happen.

23
00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.426
Rain is a real possibility.

24
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:15.052
Your turn. Say: Real possibility.

25
00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:19.563
Real possibility.

26
00:01:20.317 --> 00:01:21.364
Present simple.

27
00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.918
Present simple means the tense we use after if.

28
00:01:25.517 --> 00:01:27.493
After if we use the present simple.

29
00:01:28.083 --> 00:01:31.038
Your turn. Say: Present simple.

30
00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.122
Present simple.

31
00:01:35.883 --> 00:01:37.012
Future result.

32
00:01:38.017 --> 00:01:41.224
Future result means what will happen if the condition is true.

33
00:01:41.817 --> 00:01:43.503
Passing is a future result.

34
00:01:44.117 --> 00:01:47.059
Your turn. Say: Future result.

35
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.157
Future result.

36
00:01:51.917 --> 00:01:53.173
Unless.

37
00:01:54.183 --> 00:01:55.777
Unless means if not.

38
00:01:56.383 --> 00:01:58.418
We will go unless it rains.

39
00:01:59.017 --> 00:02:01.181
Your turn. Say: Unless.

40
00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:04.988
Unless.

41
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:06.519
Might.

42
00:02:07.517 --> 00:02:11.176
Might means used when a result is possible but not sure.

43
00:02:11.783 --> 00:02:12.959
It might rain.

44
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.691
Your turn. Say: Might.

45
00:02:18.533 --> 00:02:19.407
Might.

46
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.199
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.781
Visal, what will you do if it rains this weekend?

48
00:02:28.883 --> 00:02:39.523
If it rains, I will stay at home. The first conditional is for real possibilities in the future: if + present simple, will + base verb.

49
00:02:40.617 --> 00:02:41.989
What is unless?

50
00:02:43.083 --> 00:02:51.892
Unless means if not. We will go unless it rains means we will go if it does not rain. We use the present simple after unless too.

51
00:02:52.983 --> 00:02:54.135
Can we use might?

52
00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:07.181
Yes, might is less sure than will: If you study, you might pass. We can also change the order: We will stay at home if it rains. No comma is needed in this order.

53
00:03:08.333 --> 00:03:09.915
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:16.349
Grammar focus: First conditional: If plus present simple, will plus base verb.

55
00:03:16.649 --> 00:03:17.801
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.517 --> 00:03:20.597
If it rains, we will stay at home.

57
00:03:21.483 --> 00:03:24.098
If you study hard, you will pass the test.

58
00:03:24.983 --> 00:03:27.041
We will go out unless it rains.

59
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:37.400
Use if + present simple, will + base verb for real future possibilities. Do not use will after if. Unless means if not; might is less sure.

60
00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:41.569
Be careful! Don't say: If it will rain, we stay home.

61
00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:45.986
Say: If it rains, we will stay home.

62
00:03:46.286 --> 00:03:48.099
Use present simple after if.

63
00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.471
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:53.651
If This Happens….

65
00:03:53.951 --> 00:03:56.450
If it rains tomorrow, we will stay at home.

66
00:03:57.433 --> 00:03:59.967
If you study hard, you will pass the test.

67
00:04:00.967 --> 00:04:03.454
We won't go to the beach unless the weather is good.

68
00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:07.058
If I finish early, I might call you.

69
00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:10.821
Real possibilities need the first conditional.

70
00:04:11.933 --> 00:04:15.912
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:18.854
If it rains, we blank at home.

72
00:04:19.154 --> 00:04:22.668
A, stay. B, will stay. C, stayed.

73
00:04:26.233 --> 00:04:28.349
The answer is B: will stay.

74
00:04:29.483 --> 00:04:31.576
If you blank hard, you will pass.

75
00:04:31.876 --> 00:04:35.471
A, will study. B, study. C, studied.

76
00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:40.638
The answer is B: study.

77
00:04:41.783 --> 00:04:43.330
'Unless' means blank.

78
00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:47.295
A, if not. B, because. C, after.

79
00:04:50.833 --> 00:04:52.624
The answer is A: if not.

80
00:04:53.783 --> 00:04:55.458
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:55.758 --> 00:05:02.105
A, If it will rain, we stay.. B, If it rains, we will stay.. C, If it rained, we will stay..

82
00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:08.769
The answer is B: If it rains, we will stay..

83
00:05:09.917 --> 00:05:13.158
According to the reading, what do they need to go to the beach?

84
00:05:13.458 --> 00:05:17.007
A, good weather. B, a bus. C, money.

85
00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:22.473
The answer is A: good weather.

86
00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:26.865
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:27.717 --> 00:05:30.308
What will you do if it rains this weekend?

88
00:05:39.117 --> 00:05:40.733
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:41.033 --> 00:05:53.069
If it rains this weekend, I will stay at home and read a book. I might also cook with my mother. I use if + present simple, then will + base verb for a real possibility.

90
00:05:53.369 --> 00:05:55.101
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:56.017 --> 00:06:02.570
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and first conditional: if plus present simple, will plus base verb.

92
00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:07.415
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

93
00:06:07.715 --> 00:06:10.669
See you in Unit twenty-eight. Goodbye!

94
00:06:10.969 --> 00:06:13.888
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

